{"name":"Wasabi Ice Cream","permalink":"wasabi-ice-cream","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/WasabiIceCream.scala","source":"Kit","description":"A simple yet decadent spicy ice cream recipe, no churn needed.","tagline":null,"notes":["You can substitute wasabi for blackberries or any ingredient you fancy. Just be careful not to choose anything too watery, or you'll get ice crystals forming. It's also lovely plain.","I tend to double up this recipe to make enough for a few days.\n\nYou can use up the egg whites by making <a href=\"https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/easy-chocolate-mousse\" rel=\"nofollow\">chocolate mousse</a>."],"dated_notes":[],"tags":["Pudding"],"inherited_tags":[],"image":{"src":"https://i.reciba.se/wasabi-ice-cream.jpg","width":1080,"height":1080},"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Wasabi paste","quantity":"2 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Green food colouring","quantity":"1/2 tsp","prep":null,"notes":"optional"},{"name":"Mascarpone","quantity":"230g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Eggs","quantity":"2","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Icing Sugar","quantity":"60g","prep":null,"notes":null}]}],"method":["Carefully separate the egg yolks using your hands or spoons. Put aside the egg whites for another recipe.","Whisk the egg yolks and sugar in a bowl, with an electric mixer, until thick and light in colour.","Add the mascarpone cheese and food colouring, then continue whisking.","Add the wasabi, one teaspon at a time. Whisk thoroughly and taste each time. This makes for a hot flavour, so you may only need 1.","Decant into a freezer suitable dish and freeze for at least 6 hours."]}